      <p class="scenario-line"><strong class="label-prot">Protracted path (28%):</strong> Both sides absorb the Day 186 exchange without a further escalatory round, Hormuz remains closed, diplomatic channels stay frozen, and the conflict settles into a sustained low-transit / periodic-strike pattern through September.</p>
      <p class="scenario-line"><strong class="label-desc">De-escalation path (10%):</strong> An unobserved back-channel produces a strike pause of sufficient duration for F2 and F1 to move above their probability floor before the September 14 and September 2 horizons respectively — structurally blocked at current observed evidence.</p>
